                        "sense_id": "1d4249f0-f143-3b5f-b102-a20a26c9398c",
                        "entry_id": "6bfd99d0-5b93-3e18-a630-320c2b753707",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a funny or amusing manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae15ac76-e513-45d5-a28f-007a506d4e0d",
                                "sense_id": "1d4249f0-f143-3b5f-b102-a20a26c9398c",
                                "text": "In this respect then, Gabriel's repetitive lyric of everyone playing: “games without frontiers and war without tears” was on the one hand quite funnily wrong. 'It's a Knockout' produced tears of laughter. […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "36da7407-b709-321e-84ad-4161ad6f548f",
                        "entry_id": "6bfd99d0-5b93-3e18-a630-320c2b753707",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a strange or unexpected manner, especially of a coincidence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea826b68-02ae-4a4f-9233-88f1d371ea10",
                                "sense_id": "36da7407-b709-321e-84ad-4161ad6f548f",
                                "text": "Who, Bob? I just ran into him last week, funnily enough."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cae7d012-9888-47b0-b070-4ab99c67ca78",
                                "sense_id": "36da7407-b709-321e-84ad-4161ad6f548f",
                                "text": "It hurts to swallow and to eat . . . sometimes, I find myself breathing funnily. The doctors have not found anything, even after the X-ray, but I feel that there is something physically wrong . . ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
